  "verbalization": "Brusatol is associated with Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Brusatol to CHP-134, which in turn targets the kinase. The second pathway connects Brusatol to Hepatocyte, which is targeted by Cocosamide B, and Cocosamide B also targets the same kinase. The third pathway similarly links Brusatol to Hepatocyte, which is targeted by a different compound, [4-(1,2,2-Trimethylcyclopentyl)phenyl]methanol, which also targets the kinase. These findings suggest that Brusatol may influence the activity of the kinase through different molecular intermediates. The evidence supports a potential role for Brusatol in modulating the kinase activity, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The strength of the evidence is moderate, with varying scores across the pathways, indicating that the relationship is supported but not definitively established.",
